ges may have context that is important to consider when combined with the user's latest reply.\n\nIMPORTANT: Respond ONLY with a raw JSON object. No explanation, no commentary, no additional text, no markdown formatting, no code fences (```), no backticks.\n\nExample response (exactly this format):\n{\"chat\": 0.0, \"do\": 0.9, \"spec\": 0.1}\n\nHere is the last user message:\nVerify that if a user entry is deleted, it will set these values to NULL on delete, preventing an error","modelId":"simple-task","origin":"AI_EDITOR"}},{"assistantResponseMessage":{"content":"I will follow these instructions","toolUses":[]}},{"userInputMessage":{"content":"Verify that delete behavior is possible for the audit_log and api_usage tables, accounting for the user_id foreign key if its on\n\n<EnvironmentContext>\nThis information is provided as context about user environment. Only consider it if it's relevant to the user request ignore it otherwise.\n\n<OPEN-EDITOR-FILES>\n<file name=\".kiro/specs/database-initialization/requirements.md\" />\n<file name=\".kiro/specs/database-initialization/design.md\" />\n<file name=\".kiro/specs/database-initialization/tasks.md\" />\n<file name=\"backend/seed.py\" />\n<file name=\"backend/tests/test_database_properties.py\" />\n<file name=\"backend/requirements.txt\" />\n<file name=\"backend/database.py\" />\n<file name=\"backend/main.py\" />\n<file name=\".gitignore\" />\n</OPEN-EDITOR-FILES>\n\n<ACTIVE-EDITOR-FILE>\n<file name=\".gitignore\" />\n</ACTIVE-EDITOR-FILE>\n</EnvironmentContext>","modelId":"simple-task","origin":"AI_EDITOR"}},{"assistantResponseMessage":{"content":"Let me check the current schema and test file first.\nThe existing tests cover inserts with FK constraints but not deletes. Let me check the schema to understand the FK definitions, then write a targeted test.\nBoth tables use `NO ACTION` on delete — meaning with FK enforcement on, deleting a user that has referencing rows in `audit_log` or `api_usage` will be blocked. Dele